ChristianL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrChristianL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrChristianL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MrChristianL/Teleport-Job-Worker-Service/pulls/4","html_url":"https://github.com/MrChristianL/Teleport-Job-Worker-Service/pull/4","diff_url":"https://github.com/MrChristianL/Teleport-Job-Worker-Service/pull/4.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MrChristianL/Teleport-Job-Worker-Service/pull/4.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-13T20:43:03Z"},"body":"This PR implements the Client portion of the API as described in the approved design documentation. The gRPC client is the entry point for the end-user's CLI tool. It manages the mTLS handshake, credential loading, and the lifecycle of long-lived gRPC streams, ensuring secure and resilient communication with the remote service.\r\n\r\nKey Details:\r\n- mTLS authentication (TLS 1.3 enforced) for all outgoing requests. The client automatically manages certificate loading and verifies server identity against a trusted CA\r\n- Resilient stream management, including managing the lifecycle of long-lived gRPC streams for job output\r\n\r\nUpdates to the README have been made to reflect the core components of the Client implementation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nCurrent testing coverage for the Worker Library is **77.3%**, and is `-race` compliant.\r\n\r\nKey scenarios tested:\r\n- Non-existent job interactions\r\n- Client response to no server\r\n- Multi-client output streaming","closed_by":{"login":"MrChristianL","id":25303150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzAzMTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25303150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrChristianL","html_url":"https://github.com/MrChristianL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrChristianL